<title>BELGIUM: AT&amp;T says to close Bahrain, other offices.</title>
<headline>AT&amp;T says to close Bahrain, other offices.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. telecommunications group AT&amp;T confirmed on Thursday it plans to close its Bahrain office.</p>
<p>An AT&amp;T spokeswoman in Brussels said the closure, which takes effect September 1, was part of a wider reorganisation of AT&amp;T's network, which would also affect offices in Hungary and Ukraine.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a small number of offices,&quot; she said. &quot;We are regrouping those offices around a core competency centre.&quot;</p>
<p>The new centre could be located at an existing AT&amp;T office in Egypt or Saudi Arabia, or elsewhere. &quot;We are looking at all options,&quot; she said. A decision would be made between now and September.</p>
